{{also|druse|Druse}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|drüese}}, alongside {{m|gmh|druose}}, {{m|gmh|druos}}, from {{inh|de|goh|druos|t=swelling, swollen gland}}. The gender and stem form of the Old High German are uncertain. It was probably a masculine, so the later forms in ''-e'' continue plural forms. Alternatively (or additionally) it may have been a feminine ''i''-stem, in which case {{m|gmh||drüese}} continues the plural and oblique singular; {{m|de||druose}} (whence the doublet {{doublet|de|Druse|notext=1}}) would be a compromise form. Cognate with {{cog|osx|thrōs}}. Compare {{cog|en|dross}}.

